From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:44:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s8000, s8003: Enable PCIe storage on every
 A9 board

Every A9 board keeps its NVMe storage on the same PCIe port. The IPSW
device trees of N66, N66m, N71, N71m, N69, N69u, J71s, J72s, J71t and
J72t agree on the root complex's registers, interrupts, MSI window and
clock gates, on the storage port's PERST# (AP GPIO 160) and on the two
DARTs and the NVMMU; they differ only in phandles and in the S8003's
phy-ip window, which s8003.dtsi already describes. Enable the root
complex and both DARTs with the SoC instead of in the iPhone 6s Plus
(Samsung) and iPad 5 (TSMC) files, so storage comes up on every A9
board, the Samsung iPad 5 included.

DART 1 serves the Wi-Fi port, which every A9 board has as well; the
iPad 5 file adds that port.

Assisted-by: LLM
